## STANDING LINES (every brief)
1. **PRIOR-WORK CHECK** before each BACKLOG row, comment and the section: `git -C <root> log -S'<symbol>' --oneline -- 1_Project_Definition/CLARIFICATIONS.md` for `1eccbc8b`, `B365` (control: `C-44` returns faf2695); `/usr/bin/grep -i -n` over `BACKLOG.md`, `JIRA.md`, `history.md`, `Registers/`, `Briefs/` for every finding id and `B368`; Jira `text ~` for `B365-1` … `B365-6`. **A STATUS without a `PRIOR WORK` section naming, per finding, what you searched and found is returned unread.**
2. **No production, no deploy, no hosted site, no HTTP to any app host, no `az`, no Kudu, no docker, no Entra, no Graph.** Network: Jira (MPSCALC) and `gh api` GET under the project's `GH_CONFIG_DIR`.
3. **No message to any human.** The only client-visible words are the two allowed Jira comment texts. No mail except the coordinator's QUESTION address, no chat, no PR comment.
4. **Never delete** (`rm`, `git branch -d`, `--prune`, `gc` are forbidden; no `rm` at all). Quarantine to `.tools/_quarantine/2026-10-21_B368_<what>/`. A wrong comment gets a correcting comment and is named in Corrections.
5. **Shell:** never type `cd` (a hook refuses it); every path absolute; chains under `bash -c '...'` or a quoted heredoc; `/usr/bin/grep -i` with a positive control for every count; never an unquoted word starting with `=` in command position (the root holds a file named `=`: use `----` as a separator); Python as `python3 -I` for anything that reads a file you did not write.
6. **Verify before claiming done.** Every count in STATUS re-run at the end; Jira read-backs byte-equal (with a one-character mutant that compares unequal); the scan 0 with its control firing; no expectation edited to turn something green.
7. **No money amount, price, rate, percentage, customer, client or person's name, no `$`** in any Jira text (the allowed: shas, `file:line`, finding ids, counts of tests, rows, mutants). No new customer-facing word is written by this seat.
8. Machine load: no heavy run; Python and Jira calls only; one Jira write at a time. Launch only when load1 is under 7 (Tuesday's waiter).

